"""Present the exact N19 AC6 positive-probability certificate."""
from pathlib import Path
import html,json,re,hashlib
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;ROOT=HERE.parents[1]
def m(x,display=True):
 tag='div' if display else 'span';return f'<{tag} class="math" data-display="{str(display).lower()}" data-tex="{html.escape(x,quote=True)}"></{tag}>'
def links(items):return '<div class="proof-links">'+''.join(f'<a href="{html.escape(u,quote=True)}">{t} ↗</a>' for u,t in items)+'</div>'
def main():
 r=json.loads((HERE/'independent-verification.json').read_text());assert r['passed']
 assert r['certificateSHA256']==hashlib.sha256((HERE/'certificate.json').read_bytes()).hexdigest()
 c=json.loads((HERE/'certificate.json').read_text())['probabilityCertificate']
 css=re.search(r'<style>(.*?)</style>',(ROOT/'research/t2-qec-upper/index.html').read_text(),re.S).group(1)+'\n.math{max-width:100%;overflow-x:auto}.proof-step{border-left:3px solid #b8c9bd;padding-left:1.2rem;margin:2rem 0}.badge{color:#1c6253;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.08em}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}'
 b='<p class="eyebrow">Anticoherent states and subspaces · Exact positivity exclusion</p><a href="../../index.html#n=19&t=6">← Catalogue entry</a><h1>Nineteen qubits cannot be sixth-order anticoherent</h1>'
 b+='<div class="result"><span class="badge">Proved · arbitrary complex pure states</span>'+m(r'\boxed{K(19,t)=0\quad(t\ge6).}')+'<p>The low multipoles of a hypothetical state would force a positive linear combination of its three-copy trace and total-spin probabilities to vanish. Trace one makes that impossible. This excludes all orders six and higher. A separate four-copy certificate also excludes order five, while an exact fourth-order state attains the sharp maximum.</p></div>'
 b+='<section><h2>The exact contradiction</h2><p>For the rotationally averaged three-copy moment '+m(r'X',False)+', let '+m(r'p_J=\operatorname{Tr}(\Pi_JX)',False)+' be the probability of total spin '+m(r'J',False)+'. Every hypothetical sixth-order AC state must satisfy</p>'+m(r'\boxed{\alpha\operatorname{Tr}X+\sum_{J\in\{3/2,5/2,15/2,17/2,19/2,39/2\}}\beta_Jp_J=0.}')+'<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Coefficient</th><th>Exact positive integer</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>'+m(r'\alpha',False)+'</td><td>'+c['traceWeight']+'</td></tr>'
 for j,v in zip(c['spins2'],c['positiveWeights']):b+='<tr><td>'+m(r'\beta_{'+str(j)+'/2}',False)+'</td><td>'+str(v)+'</td></tr>'
 b+='</tbody></table></div><p>Since '+m(r'\operatorname{Tr}X=1',False)+' and '+m(r'p_J\ge0',False)+', the left side is at least '+m(r'\alpha>0',False)+'. This contradicts the identity.</p></section>'
 b+='<section><h2>Why the identity applies to every candidate</h2><div class="proof-step"><h3>1. A normalized positive moment</h3>'+m(r'X=\int_{\mathrm{SU}(2)}U_g^{\otimes3}(|\psi\rangle\langle\psi|)^{\otimes3}U_g^{\dagger\otimes3}\,dg.')+'<p>The moment is positive, has trace one and lies in '+m(r'\operatorname{Sym}^3(V_{19/2})',False)+', of dimension 1540. Rotational invariance decomposes it into 27 multiplicity blocks, with 94 real symmetric coordinates.</p></div>'
 b+='<div class="proof-step"><h3>2. Necessary contraction equations</h3><p>Sixth-order anticoherence implies</p>'+m(r'\operatorname{Tr}_1[(T_{\ell0}\otimes I^{\otimes2})X]=0,\qquad\ell=1,\ldots,6.')+'<p>Eighty-eight independent exact equations leave a six-dimensional kernel. The physical trace and total-spin probabilities are exact linear forms on this kernel. The positive integer relation above vanishes on all six kernel directions.</p></div>'
 b+='<div class="proof-step"><h3>3. Independent reconstruction</h3><p>The verifier rebuilds the spin decomposition, selected physical equations, their exact rank and complete kernel, and the trace and probabilities from all magnetic descendants. It checks the integer relation without numerical tolerances. Real angular-momentum bases allow taking real parts of the positive multiplicity matrices, preserving every equation and the trace; this covers arbitrary complex states.</p><p>No constellation symmetry, sparse Dicke support or partial-transpose assumption is needed.</p></div>'+links([('proof.tex','Complete LaTeX proof'),('certificate.json','Exact integer certificate'),('verify_independently.py','Independent standard-library verifier'),('independent-verification.json','Successful exact verification')])+'</section>'
 b+='<section><h2>The maximum pure-state order is four</h2><p>Sixth-order AC states and subspaces are impossible by this three-copy argument. The separate four-copy certificate also excludes fifth order, and the exact fourth-order representative attains the resulting maximum:</p>'+m(r'\boxed{t_{\max}(19)=4,\qquad K(19,t)=0\quad(t\ge5).}')+'<p>The fifth-order result uses a stronger moment argument; the present sixth-order proof has the simpler final contradiction in terms of total-spin probabilities.</p>'+links([('../n19-t4/index.html','Exact fourth-order state'),('../n19-t5/index.html','Fifth-order exclusion'),('../../../anticoherent-state-catalogue/index.html#n=19&t=6','Matching AC-state catalogue entry'),('../../index.html#n=19&t=5','Settled fifth-order subspace entry')])+'</section>'
 head='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>N=19: sixth-order anticoherence is impossible</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script defer src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js"></script><style>'+css+'</style><script>document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded",()=>document.querySelectorAll("[data-tex]").forEach(el=>{if(window.katex)el.innerHTML=katex.renderToString(el.dataset.tex,{displayMode:el.dataset.display==="true",throwOnError:false,strict:"ignore",trust:false});}));</script></head><body><main>'
 (HERE/'index.html').write_text(head+b+'</main></body></html>\n')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
